-- The two entry points the capstone (the Schedule K employee minimum, National Insurance Law s 348 and
-- Schedule K item 1) needs. Each declines by name wherever the Law's order or a figure is not held.
--
--   1. the full adult monthly minimum wage on a given date:
--        `the full monthly minimum wage of an employee aged 18 or over on` DAY
--      (in mw-il32-published-figures.l4: published figures, not law).
--   2. the minimum for a part-time employee on given hours:
--        `the monthly minimum wage of a part-time employee on`, below.

§ `Entry points`

@ref Minimum Wage Law s 2(a), (b) (source lines 28-29), s 1 (source line 23); the figure is published, not law
GIVEN `the employee` IS AN `An employee`
      `the day`      IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the full-time minimum wage in the unit of pay for` `the employee` `on` `the day` MEANS
    `the minimum wage under section 2(a) for` `the employee` `from` (`the full monthly minimum wage of an employee aged 18 or over on` `the day`)

@ref Minimum Wage Law s 2(b) (source line 29), s 1 (source line 23); fork F1; the figure is published, not law
GIVEN `the employee` IS AN `An employee`
      `the day`      IS A DATE
      `the work`     IS AN `Hours of work in a month`
      `the reading`  IS A `How the fraction of a position is measured`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the monthly minimum wage of a part-time employee` `the employee` `on` `the day` `working` `the work` `read` `the reading` MEANS
    `the minimum wage of a part-time position under section 2(b) for` `the employee` `from` (`the full monthly minimum wage of an employee aged 18 or over on` `the day`) `on` `the work` `read` `the reading`
